# Template for .privacy-patterns (gitignored, never commit it).
# One POSIX ERE regex per line (like `grep -E`); blank lines and lines starting with "#" are ignored.
# scripts/scan-secrets.sh checks the working tree, every unpushed commit on its own and
# their commit message, author and committer against these patterns, relative to origin/main.
# Below are generic placeholders only — fill in your own private patterns (real name,
# private mail address, host and device names, private paths, internal knowledge-base slugs, ...).
Firstname Lastname
[a-z.]+@example\.com
/ho[m]e/example-user
\[\[[a-z0-9-]+\]\]
